VALUES ('03aab094-bfdf-43e5-abab-d1b7ea953538', 'GEO.19', 3, 'numeric', 'Using the Pythagorean theorem cleverly', 'Two chords $AB$ and $AC$ of a circle start at the same point $A$ and meet at a right angle. $AB = 6$ and $AC = 8$. What is the radius of the circle?', '[]', '5', '5', 'A right angle at $A$ on the circle means that $BC$ is a diameter. By the Pythagorean theorem, $BC = \sqrt{36 + 64} = 10$, so the radius is 5.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"5","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Inscribed right angle at A: BC is a diameter = 10, radius 5.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-23T00:22:08.003Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
