VALUES ('19cbdb9c-1751-4332-9dfc-680eab249a09', 'NC26.1.SGMR.4', 2, 'numeric', 'Repeating one unit', 'Lena measures a table with one pencil. She starts at one end of the table. She lays the pencil down 8 times in all. Each time she starts where the last pencil ended. There are no gaps and no overlaps. The last pencil ends at the other end of the table. How many pencils long is the table?', '[]', '8', '8', 'Each time Lena lays the pencil down, it covers 1 pencil of the table. She lays it down 8 times, so the table is 8 pencils long.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"8","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Pencil laid 8 times end to end, no gaps or overlaps, from end to end: 8 pencils long.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-23T00:28:57.796Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
